    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Defense Evasion — Command Obfuscation (Caret)", "technique": "T1059.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-07-14 09:02:11 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 fired on WIN-LATERAL-01: process cmd.exe spawned with commandLine='cmd.exe /c w^h^o^am^i'. The caret character (^) is a cmd.exe escape character; inserted between letters it causes no change to execution but defeats naive exact-string or keyword-based detection rules that search for the string 'whoami'. Wazuh rule 92622 'CMD caret/variable obfuscation detected' fired, tagging T1059.003. Parent process was powershell.exe.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: data.win.eventdata.image=*cmd.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains '^' caret characters between command letters, data.win.eventdata.parentImage=*powershell.exe. rule.id=92622, rule.mitre.id=T1059.003.", "first_seen": "2026-07-14T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Defense Evasion — Delayed Variable Expansion Obfuscation", "technique": "T1059.003", "what_happened": "At 09:04:22 CEST, a second Sysmon Event 1 fired: cmd.exe /V /c 'set x=cmd&&!x! /c whoami'. The /V flag enables delayed variable expansion; the attacker constructs the string 'cmd' in a variable then dereferences it with !x! so the final command is 'cmd /c whoami'. Splits 'cmd' across set assignment and variable expansion to evade signature scanners looking for literal 'cmd' in a commandLine. rule.id=92622 again.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains '/V' and 'set ' and '!x!' patterns. Same parentImage=*powershell.exe, same agent WIN-LATERAL-01.", "first_seen": "2026-07-14T09:04:22+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Defense Evasion — FOR Loop Command Obfuscation", "technique": "T1059.003", "what_happened": "At 09:06:38 CEST, a third Sysmon Event 1 fired: cmd.exe /c 'FOR %i IN (w,h,o,a,m,i) DO @echo %i' piped to construct an execution loop. The FOR loop variant decomposes the target command into individual characters assembled at runtime, defeating content-based rules that tokenize on full command words. rule.id=92622 for the third time within ~4.5 minutes.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains 'FOR ' and 'DO ' and '@echo' fragments. Same agent, same parent process lineage.", "first_seen": "2026-07-14T09:06:38+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Defense Evasion + Persistence Indicator — Obfuscated .bat Script Dropped to TEMP", "technique": "T1059.003 + T1027", "what_happened": "At 09:08:09 CEST, Wazuh FIM detected a new file creation: syscheck.path=C:\\Users\\LABUSER\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\sched_helper_20260714_090809.bat. Sysmon Event 11 also fired (targetFilename containing the same path). rule.id=92623 'Obfuscated batch script execution' fired. The .bat file naming pattern 'sched_helper_<timestamp>' mimics a scheduled-task helper, a common persistence masquerading pattern (MITRE T1036). FIM held 90 seconds for the scan cycle; file content was flagged as obfuscated batch script.", "chain_reason": "syscheck.path contains 'sched_helper_' and AppData\\Local\\Temp. rule.id=92623, rule.mitre.id=T1059.003. Sysmon EID 11: data.win.eventdata.targetFilename=*sched_helper_*.bat.", "first_seen": "2026-07-14T09:08:09+0200"}
